# The native app trees. A container serves the web build; it has no use for an
# Xcode project or a Gradle wrapper, and they are the largest thing in the tree.
packages/web/ios
packages/web/android

# The rendered marketing spots — fifty megabytes of H.264 that no image stage
# copies, but that every build would otherwise ship to the daemon before the
# first layer. They are *generated*: `sites/video` is the source, and
# `assets/video/README.md` gives the `npm run build:…` lines that put them back.
# Excluded here rather than deleted because a person posting one should not have
# to install a renderer to get it.
assets/video

# The Instagram carousels — forty-four megabytes of PNG, in the same position
# as the spots above and excluded for the same reason. `sites/video/src/social`
# is the source and `assets/social/README.md` gives the one command that puts
# them back.
assets/social
